{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-17T01:18:05.331Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9a30eec154ff7d7937b394af","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3627y1","claim:pm-3fbj1f","claim:pm-wq9njf","claim:pm-ycgb5g","lineage:pm-wq9njf","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-3627y1+pm-3fbj1f+pm-wq9njf+pm-ycgb5g","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3627y1","claim:pm-3fbj1f","claim:pm-wq9njf","claim:pm-ycgb5g","lineage:pm-wq9njf","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.326","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-17T01:18:05.330Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Progress from the pm-ycgb5g branch (not closing this item): the second criterion, judging escaped JSON literals on their decoded original, is implemented for every key-named rule. decodeQuotedLiteral returns both the neutralized reading the value grammar reads and the decoded original at the same length. Capture offsets (d flag) map the matched span back, and acceptsSecretMatch then judges the original, so credential_key_assignment measures entropy on the decoded original value. The other criteria remain open: a declared adversarial corpus with a measured escape rate, and env-style all-caps keys.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-17T01:18:05.331Z"}],"before_hash":"7f1b258d38923d8015772a90f80427aeba51117c30198a07b0e347050336fa3b","after_hash":"2d66b7e13a971a43286c0d8e4c34ef9e1fad8a5de595e9e93de51517d94683df","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"fcafe2ef9699d565efe66aa8abdf0d6c9c6d5de27225ae7bee1cf0258f598284"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-17T02:43:46.889Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9a30eec154ff7d7937b394af","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.326","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-17T02:43:46.888Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Residual (4), from the CodeRabbit review of PR 1745: an escaped quoted literal followed directly by an unquoted suffix in the same value (a quoted key whose value is an escaped literal glued to eight more literal characters) has only the escaped literal judged. The suffix is never measured, and the flat rule cannot match a quoted key. Main behaves the same. Closing it needs a mixed literal model: the decoded literal's characters are data and the suffix is text with shell quoting.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-17T02:43:46.889Z"}],"before_hash":"2d66b7e13a971a43286c0d8e4c34ef9e1fad8a5de595e9e93de51517d94683df","after_hash":"827dc4d4c818e6ea9207340a79f03a58640e0ddcfab6fdc056c2918d1c7b0a1c","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4921bd59653a8bde1b1e80fc45fff94e09257050a755f42fb052f12f0ef515d6"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-17T04:53:01.573Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9a30eec154ff7d7937b394af","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.326","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-17T04:53:01.572Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Residual (5), from the CodeRabbit review of PR 1745: a password value's quoted piece ends at its first closing quote, even inside a reference, and the cut reference contributes nothing. So in a double-quoted value that holds a command reference with its own double quotes, a literal after that inner quote is not measured. Closing it needs a quoted-value scan that follows references, done in code rather than by the declared regex grammar.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-17T04:53:01.573Z"}],"before_hash":"827dc4d4c818e6ea9207340a79f03a58640e0ddcfab6fdc056c2918d1c7b0a1c","after_hash":"0acd8ed3832d6dc92b1994f193a5e8b355fe72cabe78673bf47b881207166664","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"7c5c8e29f87cdaf425e3cc66392c6327af6115012a29c515265c839cb45874de"}
